# Upstream (Arch) package names whose Package_Map outcome for the suite
# becomes a Depends of motanka-apps. packaging/build.sh resolves them with
# tools/pkgmap from packages.yaml and writes them in place of the line
# @PKGMAP_DEPENDS@ in debian/control.
#
# A plain name must have an apt or motanka outcome on every suite. A name
# written as "?name" is optional: on a suite where its outcome is skip,
# flatpak or binary it is left out (with a log line), otherwise it is a
# Depends like a plain name.
#
# The list is Upstream's install/omarchy-base.packages at the Upstream_Pin
# without the names whose packages, together with what apt installs for
# them, start a system service or change system policy. Those stay with the
# Helper (design.md, "Base package set: membership", which also gives the
# reason for each):
#   alsa-utils avahi bluez bluez-tools bluez-utils bolt cups cups-filters
#   cups-pk-helper ddcutil docker docker-buildx docker-compose gvfs-mtp
#   gvfs-nfs gvfs-smb man-db nautilus networkmanager nss-mdns
#   omarchy-power-profiles-daemon plocate qemu-user-static-binfmt sushi
#   system-config-printer ufw
# herdr is not listed: motanka-apps ships its binary itself. inetutils is
# not listed either: its outcome is hostname, an Essential package that is on
# every Ubuntu system, and Debian policy forbids an unversioned Depends on it.
base-devel
bash-completion
bat
brightnessctl
btop
dosfstools
dotnet-runtime
evince
exfatprogs
eza
